result:
I found no blocking issues. I couldn't find any SOAP or REST request that writes or reaches another host and still passes the allowlist, or any route by which the password or session id leaks. There are two minor advisories.

```
VERDICT: PASS
CANDIDATE: 525b7a85336bbd0b641b0419c899e791abf791d6
FINDING faultcode-echo advisory: the server's SOAP faultcode is copied into the error detail and printed to stderr (`crm-migrate: error code=soap_fault ... detail=faultcode=<value>`). Any value matching `[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_.:-]{0,63}` is accepted, so a secret-shaped string would be printed. Only the TLS-verified login host or the configured origin could send one, and real Salesforce faultcodes come from a fixed set, so there is no plausible way to exploit this | evidence: migrate/lib/crm_migrate/auth_soap.py:49 and :277-287; my probe p2 sent a 500 fault with `<faultcode>`=FAKE_PASSWORD (no default namespace), giving rc=4 with the sentinel password on stderr. The faultstring is correctly never read | expected: accept only `(?:soapenv:|sf:)?[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]{0,63}` (or a list of known codes), otherwise use UNKNOWN, and add a sentinel test where the faultcode is the password
FINDING surrogate-credential advisory: a lone UTF-16 surrogate in the stdin JSON (`"\ud800"`) passes read_stdin_credentials and _check_credential. render_login_body then raises an uncaught UnicodeEncodeError, so the run ends with rc=1 "internal error (UnicodeEncodeError)" instead of a clean ConfigError. Nothing is sent and nothing leaks, because only the class name is printed | evidence: auth_soap.py:93-108, cli.py read_stdin_credentials; probe p2 "surrogate-pw" gave rc=1, leak=[] | expected: in _check_credential, refuse any value that does not encode as strict UTF-8, giving `credentials_invalid`
EVIDENCE:
- `git -C <wt> rev-parse HEAD` = 525b7a85…; `git status --porcelain` was empty at the start and at the end. Base..HEAD has 2 commits and 20 files, all inside the WO scope allowlist (checked with grep -v against the allowlist; nothing outside it).
- `gitleaks git --log-opts="98f10ff..525b7a8" --redact --no-banner <wt>`: 2 commits scanned, no leaks found. Grepping the diff for URLs and emails found only example.test, my.salesforce.com patterns and github.com placeholders, with no personal data.
- Dependencies: every new import is from the standard library (xml.parsers.expat, xml.sax.saxutils, hashlib, json, …). The image is unchanged and digest-pinned. No downloads or install scripts.
- Tests: `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests/migrate -t <wt>` ran 237 tests: OK, 1 skipped. `bash -n scripts/migrate.sh` passed. shellcheck is not installed.
- Blocking fix soap-dtd-utf16-bypass is verified (probe p1, 24 parse cases). Refused: UTF-16 LE/BE with and without BOM, UTF-32, a space then UTF-16, EBCDIC/cp037, UTF-7, ISO-8859-1 declarations, a single-quoted utf-16 declaration, a UTF-8 BOM followed by a utf-16 declaration, a double BOM, overlong `\xc0\xbc`, NUL, lowercase doctype, a duplicate encoding attribute, a leading-space declaration, and depth 20000 (size limit). Layer 3 on its own (_HardenedXMLParser with layers 1 and 2 bypassed) refuses DOCTYPE, an internal entity, a parameter entity and an external SYSTEM DTD with soap_dtd_refused. XInclude, processing instructions and character refs parse but are inert under ElementTree.
- Allowlist (probe p1, 37 requests): only the legitimate login and logout requests pass. Refused:
  - logout sent to the login host, login sent to the origin;
  - a login body on the logout path, the login action on the logout path;
  - delete, delete+logout in one Body, setPassword, an extra SOAP header, trailing whitespace or a comment after the template;
  - the Soap/s (Apex), Soap/m (metadata) and Soap/T (tooling) endpoints and lowercase /soap/;
  - an injected Host header, a quoted SOAPAction, an uppercase host, a trailing-dot host, :443, userinfo, a foreign host;
  - PUT, PATCH to sobjects, POST to composite, GET to apexrest, GET to a Soap path;
  - a UTF-16 login body, a namespace prefix change, a bytes header name, CRLF in a header, a fragment, a tab in the URL, an ideographic-dot hostname.

  Bodies are re-rendered and compared byte for byte against the fixed templates (auth_soap.py:234-268). The transport repeats policy.check before connecting and uses http.client with no proxy or redirect.
- Secrets (probe p2, cli.main end to end with in-process fake, checking stdout, stderr, logs and every output file): no leak for a valid run, a control character, a duplicate key, bad JSON, a non-string value, an over-long value, non-UTF-8 stdin, a namespaced fault containing the password, a session-shaped password echo, a serverUrl made of the session id, a DTD response, or a 302. The one leak is the faultcode echo above. Request repr and str are redacted (messages.py:15-23), as is SoapSession repr. The catch-all prints only the class name. Logout failures log only the class name and never change the exit code.
- Legacy env (probe p3):
  - an empty or missing CRM_LEGACY_ENV_FILE gives "not configured", so it fails closed;
  - `""` and relative paths are refused;
  - `$(...)`, backticks and trailing text after a quote are refused, and the error messages contain no values;
  - a valid file writes only the JSON to stdout;
  - a group-writable file and a symlinked path are refused.

  migrate.sh never puts the values into a shell variable, argv or the environment (hostcheck output is piped straight to `docker compose run -T`). It fingerprints sha256, mtime, size and inode before and after the run, and exits 22 on a change.
- Base advisories: every validator now uses \A…\Z or fullmatch. The only `$`-anchored re.match calls left are in the synthetic fake's request routing (synthetic.py:526, :596), which is not a validator. check_runtime_path now also compares against realpath, so it rejects a symlinked runtime directory. docs/MIGRATION.md has a "Network egress" section saying the bridge network does not restrict egress and naming the extra login host.
- Isolation: nothing writes outside the run directory. The script does not touch git hooks, git config, CI or ForgeV2 files. The waiver applies only when auth_mode=="soap-legacy" (metadata.py run_gate, client.set_write_waiver).
```
